                                                "sense_id": "d8b7c1cf-3c32-3f10-9a32-b3ff936c1b2d",
                                                "text": "Who ever ſaw a noble ſight, / That never view'd a brave Sea Fight: / Hang up your bloody Colours in the Aire, / Up with your Fights, and your Nettings prepare, / Your Merry Mates chear, with a luſty bold ſpright, / Now each Man his brindice, and then to the Fight, […]"
