                                                "sense_id": "d8b7c1cf-3c32-3f10-9a32-b3ff936c1b2d",
                                                "text": "The term \"radar netting\" (fig 43) describes the process by which track data derived from several additional or remote radars are gathered at a single center to produce an integrated set of meaningful target information which can be distributed to all AD elements concerned. … Radar netting can provide concurrent coverage of a selected area by more than one radar."
